%I A398541 #19 Aug 14 2026 14:07:36
%S A398541 3,9,13,22,11,49,57,65,19,112,45,158,27,225,241
%N A398541 Least k such that every {+1,-1}-coloring of {1,...,k} contains an n-term arithmetic progression whose signed sum has absolute value >= 2.
%C A398541 a(n) is the quantity N(n,2) of Erdős Problem #176. Values for odd n <= 11 were first published by M. J. Goss, Jr. (2026). All terms a(2)..a(12) carry machine-checkable DRAT UNSAT certificates plus witness colorings. a(n) <= A005346(n) (the van der Waerden number W(2,n)), since a monochromatic n-term arithmetic progression has |sum| = n >= 2. a(13) = 158 first computed 2026-08-02 (cube-and-conquer UNSAT proof, 4096 drat-trim-verified certificates; T. A. Lystad). a(14) = 27 from the parity formula (even k; Spencer 1973); a(15) = 225 first computed 2026-08-02 (kissat UNSAT proof, drat-trim-verified certificate; T. A. Lystad).
%D A398541 J. Spencer, Solution to Problem P.185, Bull. Canad. Math. Soc. 16 (1973), 464.
%H A398541 T. F. Bloom, <a href="https://www.erdosproblems.com/176">Erdős Problem #176</a>.
%H A398541 M. J. Goss, Jr., <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20763838">The Parity Collapse and Entropy Drain: First Bounds on Erdős's Discrepancy Threshold N(k,2)</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%H A398541 T. A. Lystad, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21739847">Erdős Problem 176 — exact small values of the discrepancy threshold N(k,2) with machine-checkable DRAT certificates</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%H A398541 T. A. Lystad, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21756090">Erdős Problem 176 — exact small values of the discrepancy threshold N(k,2) with machine-checkable DRAT certificates (v1.1: N(13,2) = 158)</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%H A398541 T. A. Lystad, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21761884">Erdős Problem 176 — exact small values of the discrepancy threshold N(k,2) with machine-checkable DRAT certificates (v1.2: N(15,2) = 225)</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%H A398541 J. Spencer, <a href="https://doi.org/10.4153/cmb-1972-009-x">A Remark on Coloring Integers</a>, Canad. Math. Bull. 15 (1972), 43-44.
%F A398541 For t >= 1 and m odd, a(2^t*m) = 2^t*(2^t*m - 1) + 1 (parity argument; Spencer 1973).
%e A398541 a(3) = 9: the coloring --++--++ of {1,...,8} has no 3-term arithmetic progression with |sum| >= 2, but every {+1,-1}-coloring of {1,...,9} has one (machine-checked).
%e A398541 a(12) = 45 = 4*11 + 1 from the formula with t = 2, m = 3.
%Y A398541 Cf. A005346 (van der Waerden numbers W(2,n)), A121894, A237695 (maximum length of a +-1 sequence of discrepancy n), A181740.
%K A398541 nonn,hard,more,changed
%O A398541 2,1
%A A398541 _T. Alexander Lystad_, Aug 01 2026
%E A398541 a(16) from _Leo Y. Zhang_, Aug 13 2026
